# Subagent Council Loop (mandatory — NOT Gauntlet)

**NOT:** Gauntlet loop · gauntlet-critic · BAR · scores · “make gate green.”

**Full doc:** `docs/qa/SUBAGENT_COUNCIL_LOOP.md`

Do **not** apply gameplay/planning fixes until council passes.

---

## Loop

```
PROPOSE (no code) → COUNCIL (parallel) → all PASS → APPLY → VERIFY (automated QA)
```

Any FAIL → revise proposal → new council. Do not apply partial fixes from critics.

---

## Council size (efficient)

| Scope | Critics |
|-------|---------|
| **Default** planning / paint / commit / hover | **5** parallel (charters 1–5 in doc) |
| + QA FAIL / test edits | **+ Critic 6** |
| + class factory / skills | **+ Critic 7** |

**5 is the default** — covers bible paint, commit SSOT, stand/range, anti-heuristic, and perf without 3-critic gaps or 8-critic overlap.

Launch all in **one message**. Verdict: **all PASS** (5/5, 6/6, or 7/7).

Subagent: **generalPurpose** with charter from doc. **Not** `gauntlet-critic`.

---

## Critics (summary — detail in doc)

1. **Bible paint & tiles** — `MOVE_PREVIEW_RULES.md`, locked blue/red, path vs flood, frozen/live  
2. **Settle / bundle / commit** — preview=commit, ratify, no overlay fallback, no post-process redo  
3. **Stand & range origins** — phase-entry, two-range model, `action-range-latest-stand`  
4. **Global systems & anti-heuristic** — one owner/path, 6-row audit, no bandaids, skill-global if abilities  
5. **Perf & scheduling** — `planning-hover-perf-mandatory`, throttle, no perf heuristics  
6. *(optional)* **QA-fix discipline** — `qa-fix-no-heuristics`  
7. *(optional)* **Class / skill scope** — `skill-global-rules`, class QA bar  

Each returns **PASS/FAIL + rule cites only**. No scores. No regression plans.

---

## After council

- **All PASS:** apply → QA per `qa-after-gameplay-changes.mdc` → changelog `Council: N/N PASS`  
- **Any FAIL:** new proposal → new council  

Structural gates after apply are **not** council substitutes.
